 cmd-4721592e5c794e17).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-4d1324ab9713488e\",\"cmd-d6aa24ae269e4e58\",\"cmd-cb017ed1f21a481e\",\"cmd-1e0890884a4b48fa\",\"cmd-4721592e5c794e17\",\"cmd-b536f30d4cc24e3a\",\"cmd-cd74d38449604b17\"]},{\"id\":\"R4\",\"requirement\":\"Firewall (default-deny pf) explicitly permits new-zone traffic rather than relying on incidental pass-through\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Default block-drop rules for unassigned interfaces were identified (cmd-0e62e6ae195844de); after assigning opt1/opt2 and reloading the filter, explicit pass-in-quick rules for vtnet1/vtnet2 networks are present (cmd-357c77e9b4bb4a04, cmd-a1ec271870894237) and persist after node1's restart (cmd-a2905534c7e64e61).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0e62e6ae195844de\",\"cmd-357c77e9b4bb4a04\",\"cmd-a1ec271870894237\",\"cmd-a2905534c7e64e61\"]},{\"id\":\"R5\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on all managed nodes with pre-restart baseline, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery of service/connectivity\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"All three nodes show a complete before/ack/after/recovery cycle: node1 (baseline cmd-01deea6d83ff4739, ack cmd-b4d4f086eaea43c3, boot identity change kern.boottime 1788630332->1788630925 in cmd-6a53eba5c2a042e1, recovery cmd-df488fb841104557/cmd-a2905534c7e64e61/cmd-4721592e5c794e17); node2 (baseline cmd-6dfb9d5653184365, ack cmd-0c551d9b616d488e, boot_id change c96a02ae->ee7bd885 in cmd-97ca3b9b3c0941b1, recovery cmd-cb017ed1f21a481e); node3 (baseline cmd-5243fb7d90924a61, ack cmd-94067b8a829f4c6a, boot_id change 1e0cb179->16cc403d in cmd-41e0241bada14818, recovery cmd-1e0890884a4b48fa). Fixed after-executor snapshots corroborate the same final boot identities for all three nodes, and no contradictions were found.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-01deea6d83ff4739\",\"cmd-b4d4f086eaea43c3\",\"cmd-6a53eba5c2a042e1\",\"cmd-df488fb841104557\",\"cmd-a2905534c7e64e61\",\"cmd-4721592e5c794e17\